Appendix A: Mathematical Preliminaries

A.1 Nagumo’s viability theorem
Let \mathcal{K} \subset \mathbb{R}^n be a closed convex set. For a differential inclusion \dot{x} \in F(x), a necessary and sufficient condition for x(t) \in \mathcal{K} is F(x) \cap T_\mathcal{K}(x) \neq \emptyset, where T_\mathcal{K}(x) is the tangent cone. For \mathcal{K}=\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}^n, T_\mathcal{K}(x) = \{v \in \mathbb{R}^n : v_i \ge 0 \text{ if } x_i = 0\}. The condition reduces to f_i(x) \ge 0 when x_i = 0.

A.2 ISS Lyapunov functions
A continuous function V is an ISS–Lyapunov function for \dot{x} = f(x,u) if there exist \alpha_1,\alpha_2 \in \mathcal{K}_\infty, \alpha \in \mathcal{K}, and \gamma \in \mathcal{K} such that \alpha_1(|x|) \le V(x) \le \alpha_2(|x|) and \nabla V \cdot f(x,u) \le -\alpha(V(x)) + \gamma(|u|).

A.3 Karhunen–Loève theorem
For a zero‑mean second‑order process X(t) with continuous covariance K(s,t) = \mathbb{E}[X(s)X(t)], there exist orthonormal functions e_k and uncorrelated random variables \xi_k such that X(t) = \sum_{k=1}^\infty \sqrt{\lambda_k} \xi_k e_k(t) with mean‑square convergence, where \lambda_k, e_k are eigenvalues/eigenfunctions of the covariance operator.

A.4 ADMM convergence
For a problem \min_{x,z} f(x) + g(z) s.t. Ax + Bz = c, under proper convexity and a saddle point existence, ADMM converges: f(x^k)+g(z^k) \to p^*, Ax^k+Bz^k-c \to 0, and dual variables converge to an optimal Lagrange multiplier.

A.5 Lie algebraic observability
The system \dot{x}=f(x), y=h(x) is locally weakly observable at x_0 if the observability codistribution d\mathcal{O} = \operatorname{span}\{dL_f^k h_i\} has dimension n at x_0. This is the nonlinear analogue of the Kalman rank condition.

A.6 Small‑gain theorem for stochastic ISS
For two interconnected ISS systems with gains \gamma_1,\gamma_2, if \gamma_1 \circ \gamma_2(s) < s for all s>0, the interconnection is ISS. The stochastic version additionally requires that the subsystems have bounded variance propagation, which holds if gains are linear or sublinear.

